    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nVernegly is an A rated contemporary bungalow, designed with modern family living in mind\n\nSet behind electric gates, the house combines clean architectural lines with a warm, comfortable interior, while the coastal setting places a selection of beaches within easy reach, including Bannow Island, The Long Gap, Blackhall Strand and Cockle Strand, with Cullenstown Beach approximately 5 km from the property.\n\nThe accommodation is arranged over a single level and is both well balanced and highly functional, comprising an open plan kitchen/dining/living area, a separate sitting room, utility, office, three bedrooms and three bathrooms, together with an integral garage.\n\nOn arrival, the property is entered via a bright entrance hallway which immediately establishes the contemporary tone. A long, narrow corridor runs the full length of the house, finished with a sleek polished concrete floor, creating a strong sense of perspective and an effortless connection between the main living spaces and bedroom accommodation.\n\nThe heart of the home is an impressive open plan kitchen, dining and living area, positioned to take full advantage of its south-facing, triple aspect orientation. This is a notably light-filled space, with patio doors opening directly to the garden, making it ideal for everyday living and entertaining alike. The kitchen is centred around a generous island, complemented by bespoke, custom-made cabinetry, resulting in a space that is both practical and design-led.\n\nJust off the main hall is a fully fitted utility room, complete with sink, washing machine and tumble dryer, and discreetly accommodating the CCTV monitor. A dedicated coat closet/boot room, fitted with sensor lighting, provides excellent day-to-day storage.\n\nA separate sitting room offers a quieter, more relaxed setting, with an electric fire providing ambience and comfort. The bedroom accommodation is thoughtfully arranged. The master bedroom suite benefits from a walk-in wardrobe and an en suite. Two further double bedrooms are served by a well-appointed Jack & Jill bathroom, featuring a free-standing bath, adding a touch of luxury and practicality for family life. An additional office provides valuable flexibility for remote working, study or hobby use.\n\nCompleted in 2020, the specification is particularly impressive, combining refined finishes with practical technology. Each bathroom is fitted with heated mirrors with integrated LED lighting, while sensor lighting is incorporated throughout the house including the Jack & Jill bathroom, main bathroom, garage, utility room and walk-in wardrobe, together with external sensor lighting. Security has been carefully considered with CCTV, burglar and fire alarms, and a changeover switch for a generator. The garage is fitted with an electric roller shutter, and externally there are covered electric sockets and outdoor taps, ideal for outdoor use and maintenance."
      },
      {
